1. Introduction

Welcome to T-Office, your comprehensive internal office management platform. This guide will help you understand and utilize all the features available in the application to streamline your daily work processes.

T-Office is designed to centralize administrative, HR, inventory, and collaboration workflows within your organization, making it easier to manage tasks, communicate with colleagues, and track important information.

2. Getting Started

To access T-Office:
1. Open your web browser and navigate to the T-Office URL provided by your administrator
2. Enter your username and password to log in
3. Upon successful authentication, you'll be directed to your personalized dashboard

If you don't have an account yet, contact your system administrator to create one for you.

3. Main Features

3.1 Dashboard

The Dashboard serves as your central hub for all activities within T-Office.

Key Features:
• Activity Feed: See recent activities and system events relevant to you
• Quick Stats: View key metrics and statistics
• Navigation Hub: Easy access to all sections of the application

The dashboard provides a personalized overview of your work environment and helps you stay informed about important updates.

3.2 Chat

The Chat module enables internal team communication with privacy features.

Key Features:
• Send and receive messages anonymously
• Moderator Mode: Send messages with special privileges (if authorized)
• Chat History: Review past conversations
• Summarizer: Generate key points from previous discussions
• Pause/Resume Chat: Temporarily stop chat activities
• Clear Chat: Remove all messages from the chat (if authorized)

This feature promotes collaborative work while maintaining professional communication standards.

3.3 Clock & Attendance

Track your work hours and manage attendance with the Clock module.

Key Features:
• Clock In/Out: Record your work hours with timestamp logging
• Location Management:
  - Add Location: Save office locations
  - Delete Location: Remove saved locations
  - View Locations: See all your saved locations
• Map View: Visualize your current location relative to office locations
• Attendance History: Review your past clock-in/clock-out records
• Reports: Access attendance summaries (managers only)

This system helps ensure accurate time tracking for payroll and productivity analysis.

3.4 Profile Management

Manage your personal information and documents in the Profile section.

Key Features:
• Personal Information: View and update your contact details
• Certifications: View and manage your professional certificates
• Account Status: Check your current account standing
• HR Queries: View responses to queries submitted to HR
• Scheduled Inductions: View upcoming induction sessions you're registered for

Keep your profile updated to ensure accurate communication and record-keeping.

3.5 Settings

Customize your application experience in the Settings section.

Key Features:
• Theme Selection: Choose between light and dark display modes

Adjust these settings to create a comfortable working environment.

3.6 HR Management

The HR Management section provides tools for human resources operations and is divided into three sub-sections:

3.6.1 Onboarding
Manage employee onboarding processes:
• Create New Users: Add new employee accounts to the system (HR/Admin only)
• Schedule Inductions: Plan onboarding sessions for new employees across multiple departments
• View Inductions: See all scheduled induction sessions with details
• Delete Inductions: Cancel planned induction sessions (HR/Admin only)

3.6.2 Queries
Handle HR-related questions and communications:
• Send Queries: Submit questions or concerns to the HR department
• View Query History: Review past communications with HR and their resolutions
• Reply Queries: Provide responses to HR queries responded to by the Quried User

3.6.3 Users
Manage employee information and records:
• View User Details: Access employee information and profiles (HR/Admin only)
• Edit User Information: Update employee details
• Deactivate Accounts: Temporarily disable employee accounts

This module streamlines employee onboarding and HR communication processes.

3.7 Admin Panel

Administrative controls for managing the entire system (Admin users only).

Key Features:
• Database Management: View and manage system data
• User Administration: Manage accounts, roles, and permissions
• System Logs: Monitor application activities and security events
• Features Documentation: Access comprehensive system information
• Department Management: Create and manage departments and roles
• Feature Access Control: Configure which features each department can access

The Admin Panel provides complete control over the T-Office environment.

3.8 Approvals

Handle certificate and document approval requests.

Key Features:
• Accept/Reject Certificate Approvals: Process certification requests from employees

This streamlined approval process ensures proper documentation validation.

3.9 Inventory Management

Comprehensive product and stock management system with four sub-sections:

3.9.1 Products
Manage your product catalog:
• View Product List: See all products in the inventory
• Add New Products: Create entries for new items
• Edit Product Information: Update product details
• Delete Products: Remove items from the catalog
• Import Products: Bulk upload product data via CSV
• Export Product List: Download product data as CSV
• View Product Details: See comprehensive information about specific products

3.9.2 Inbound
Track incoming inventory shipments:
• View Inbound Transactions: See all incoming shipments
• Add New Inbound Transaction: Record new incoming shipments
• Edit Inbound Details: Update shipment information
• Delete Inbound Records: Remove incorrect entries
• Mark as Stored: Move received items to storage
• Export Inbound Data: Download inbound transaction data as CSV

3.9.3 Store
Manage stored inventory:
• View Stored Items: See all items currently in storage
• Edit Storage Details: Update storage information
• Delete Storage Records: Remove items from storage
• Create Outbound Request: Initiate shipment of stored items
• Export Storage Data: Download stored inventory data as CSV

3.9.4 Outbound
Process outgoing inventory requests:
• View Outbound Transactions: See all outgoing shipments
• Mark as Dispatched: Record when items are sent
• Mark as Delivered: Record when items are received
• Delete Outbound Records: Remove incorrect entries
• Export Outbound Data: Download outbound transaction data as CSV

This system provides complete visibility into inventory movements and stock levels.

3.10 Resources & Wiki

Access and contribute to department-specific knowledge bases with two sub-sections:

3.10.1 Wiki
Access department-specific documentation:
• View Topics: Browse available documentation for your department
• Search Wiki: Find specific information using search functionality
• Read Articles: Access detailed guides and procedures

3.10.2 Create
Contribute to the knowledge base (if authorized):
• Create New Topics: Add new documentation articles
• Edit Existing Topics: Update current documentation
• Delete Topics: Remove outdated information

The Wiki promotes knowledge sharing and ensures important information is readily available.

4. Conclusion

T-Office is designed to enhance productivity and streamline workplace processes. By leveraging its comprehensive feature set, you can efficiently manage your daily tasks, collaborate with colleagues, and maintain accurate records.

For technical support or questions about specific features, please contact your system administrator.

Regular updates and improvements to T-Office ensure you always have access to the latest tools for workplace efficiency.